      "content": "the metaphors are a bit distracting, can we stick to the technical side? i don't have access to Valgrind on this specific hardware, it's a bare-metal environment. what are some specific C++ patterns or common mistakes in embedded systems that could cause a slow, gradual exhaustion of heap memory without it being a straightforward missing 'delete'?",
