      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks. regarding point 5, a lot of our objects use smart pointers to manage lifecycles. is it possible for shared_ptr to cause this kind of gradual exhaustion? also, are there any other specific ways that object ownership can get messed up in a multi-threaded embedded context that would look like a slow leak?",
      "source": "evaluator"
